-- src:1538 | (4) If the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated, and the Court gives judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed, and no provision is made by the judgment as to how the damages are to be assessed, the damages must, subject to the provisions of this Rule, be assessed by the Registrar or Judge, and the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment must, within one month from the date of the judgment, apply to the Court for directions and the provisions of Order 9, Rule 25(12) apply to the application for directions.
@ref O 15 r 15(4) (src:1538)
`o 15 r 15(4) the period after the judgment for applying for directions` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 1
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1539 | (5) On the hearing of the application for directions mentioned in paragraph (4), the Court may give directions as to the time by which a notice of appointment for assessment of damages must be filed and such notice upon being filed must be served not later than 14 days after the date of filing on the party against whom the judgment is given.
@ref O 15 r 15(5) (src:1539)
`o 15 r 15(5) the period after the date of filing for serving the notice of appointment` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1538 | (4) If the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated, and the Court gives judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed, and no provision is made by the judgment as to how the damages are to be assessed, the damages must, subject to the provisions of this Rule, be assessed by the Registrar or Judge, and the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment must, within one month from the date of the judgment, apply to the Court for directions and the provisions of Order 9, Rule 25(12) apply to the application for directions.
@ref O 15 r 15(4) (src:1538)
GIVEN `the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court gave judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment makes provision as to how the damages are to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 15(4) the damages must be assessed by the Registrar or Judge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated` AND `the Court gave judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed` AND (NOT `the judgment makes provision as to how the damages are to be assessed`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated, and the Court gives judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed, and no provision is made by the judgment as to how the damages are to be assessed" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

@ref O 15 r 15(4) (src:1538)
GIVEN `the date the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment applied to the Court for directions` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 15(4) the application for directions is made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment applied to the Court for directions` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month from the date of the judgment" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

@ref O 15 r 15(4) (src:1538)
GIVEN `the application is the application for directions mentioned in paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 15(4) the provisions of Order 9, Rule 25(12) apply to the application for directions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is the application for directions mentioned in paragraph (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the provisions of Order 9, Rule 25(12) apply to the application for directions"

@ref O 15 r 15(4) (src:1538)
GIVEN `the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court gave judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment makes provision as to how the damages are to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 15(4) the party must apply to the Court for directions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated`) OR (NOT `the Court gave judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed`) OR `the judgment makes provision as to how the damages are to be assessed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the hearing was ordered to be bifurcated, and the Court gives judgment on liability and for damages to be assessed, and no provision is made by the judgment as to how the damages are to be assessed" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)
        IF (NOT `the person is the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

