-- src:1560 | (9) If the statements to be admitted pursuant to section 32 of the Evidence Act are contained in a document, the notice in paragraph (7) must contain the following: ( a )
-- src:1561 | the time and place at which the statements were made;
-- src:1562 | ( b )
-- src:1563 | the name of the maker and his or her address, if known;
-- src:1564 | ( c )
-- src:1565 | if the maker has passed away, the date of death, if known;
-- src:1566 | ( d )
-- src:1567 | if the maker of the document is different from the maker of the statements, the name of the maker of the document and his or her address, if known;
-- src:1568 | ( e )
-- src:1569 | if the maker of the document has passed away, the date of death, if known;
-- src:1570 | ( f )
-- src:1571 | a copy of the document or the relevant part of that document.
@ref O 15 r 16(9) (src:1560-1571)
GIVEN `the notice states the time and place at which the statements were made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the maker and his or her address, if known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker has passed away` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date of death, if known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker of the document is different from the maker of the statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the maker of the document and his or her address, if known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker of the document has passed away` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date of death of the maker of the document, if known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice encloses a copy of the document or the relevant part of that document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 15 r 16(9) the notice for statements contained in a document contains what the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice states the time and place at which the statements were made` AND `the notice states the name of the maker and his or her address, if known` AND ((NOT `the maker has passed away`) OR `the notice states the date of death, if known`) AND ((NOT `the maker of the document is different from the maker of the statements`) OR `the notice states the name of the maker of the document and his or her address, if known`) AND ((NOT `the maker of the document has passed away`) OR `the notice states the date of death of the maker of the document, if known`) AND `the notice encloses a copy of the document or the relevant part of that document` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice in paragraph (7) must contain the following" (a requirement of content read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

